WEBVTT

00:04.470 --> 00:07.932
Good morning, Class 6-1!

00:08.349 --> 00:09.976
Good morning!

00:10.768 --> 00:13.812
Welcome to the playtest

00:13.813 --> 00:18.066
of the world's first fulldive VRMMORPG
from IO-TAGE Inc,

00:18.067 --> 00:21.695
Actual Magic.

00:21.696 --> 00:23.948
Thank you very much for joining us today.

00:25.533 --> 00:30.454
Does everyone have their QREST,
i-Lenses, and earpieces on?

00:30.455 --> 00:31.705
Oh, crap!

00:31.706 --> 00:33.207
I forgot too.

00:41.549 --> 00:43.176
There we go.

00:43.801 --> 00:46.678
Now, open your QREST menus

00:46.679 --> 00:48.723
and confirm the message.

00:50.600 --> 00:52.226
ACTUAL MAGIC
CLIENT INSTALLED

00:52.810 --> 00:56.272
That's the Actual Magic client program.

00:57.315 --> 01:01.152
Please note that
it cannot be launched at this time.

01:02.570 --> 01:04.113
WARNING: PERMISSION REQUIRED

01:08.201 --> 01:13.371
You will now proceed to Playroom 1
on the second floor

01:13.372 --> 01:17.125
and enter your Caliculus,
a biocommunication capsule unit

01:17.126 --> 01:20.838
that will allow you to enter
the world of Actual Magic.

01:23.591 --> 01:28.386
First, we will perform a full-body scan
to create your avatar.

01:28.387 --> 01:31.723
To allow the scan to capture
the finer details of your body,

01:31.724 --> 01:35.102
please remain as still as possible
until the process is complete.

01:36.062 --> 01:38.730
Further instructions
for the remaining steps

01:38.731 --> 01:41.150
will be provided inside the Caliculus.

01:42.026 --> 01:45.446
The playtest is scheduled
to last three hours.

01:46.239 --> 01:48.782
Like I said this morning,

01:48.783 --> 01:51.702
I want you all to follow
proper in-game etiquette!

02:03.506 --> 02:06.259
Watamaki?

03:41.312 --> 03:42.939
DEVILS' CREST

03:43.606 --> 03:47.526
EPISODE 2: TRANSFORMATION

03:57.036 --> 03:58.704
Watamaki, is that you?

04:07.630 --> 04:11.341
Run, Yu! Get outside
and bring back some adults!

04:11.342 --> 04:12.677
Konken.

04:26.816 --> 04:29.734
What are you doing, Yu? Get outside!

04:29.735 --> 04:31.737
Like I could run and leave you behind!

04:39.203 --> 04:40.079
Yu!

04:57.221 --> 04:58.388
Yu!

04:58.389 --> 04:59.390
Flamma!

05:01.892 --> 05:02.977
Sagitta!

05:03.894 --> 05:05.062
Ignis!

05:05.646 --> 05:07.356
Flame Arrow!

05:14.947 --> 05:16.198
Sawa?

05:19.201 --> 05:22.203
Yuumy, launch Actual Magic!

05:22.204 --> 05:23.872
- What?
- Hurry!

05:23.873 --> 05:25.249
Okay.

05:55.446 --> 05:57.363
ALTHEA 2F - PLAYROOM 01

05:57.364 --> 05:59.867
YUMA ASHIHARA

06:03.954 --> 06:05.873
SAWA ASHIHARA

06:06.665 --> 06:07.582
Why?

06:07.583 --> 06:09.876
- Are we still in the--
- This is real.

06:09.877 --> 06:12.379
If you die, you die for real!

06:16.717 --> 06:18.636
SUMIKA WATAMAKI

06:21.222 --> 06:24.058
It'll take another 30 seconds
before I can cast again.

06:24.767 --> 06:26.226
Hold her off until then!

06:26.227 --> 06:28.144
We need her HP down into the red!

06:28.145 --> 06:29.562
Hold her off?

06:29.563 --> 06:30.773
Here she comes!

06:41.325 --> 06:42.784
How did I...

06:42.785 --> 06:44.537
Your stats have gone up!

06:45.121 --> 06:47.164
Keep it up and buy us some more time!

07:02.304 --> 07:03.972
Get back! Flamma!

07:03.973 --> 07:05.849
Wait. Don't kill her.

07:05.850 --> 07:06.766
SUMIKA WATAMAKI

07:06.767 --> 07:08.434
What are you saying?

07:08.435 --> 07:11.480
If we don't kill her,
she'll just keep attacking us!

07:30.291 --> 07:31.333
What's wrong?

07:32.585 --> 07:33.877
Watamaki!

07:33.878 --> 07:35.462
Are you looking for something?

07:36.130 --> 07:39.132
I dropped my i-Lens.

07:39.133 --> 07:41.635
Are you sure it didn't
just shift out of place?

07:42.678 --> 07:45.222
No, you're right. It's not in there.

07:46.182 --> 07:47.640
I'll help you look.

07:47.641 --> 07:49.225
No, that's okay, I...

07:49.226 --> 07:50.728
Don't worry about it.

07:51.896 --> 07:53.230
Gimme your hand for a sec.

07:57.193 --> 07:58.611
LOCATE DEVICE

08:05.034 --> 08:06.243
There it is!

08:11.790 --> 08:14.709
Thank you. But how did you...

08:14.710 --> 08:18.296
QRESTs have a feature
for locating i-Lenses and earpieces

08:18.297 --> 08:20.173
if you drop them.

08:20.174 --> 08:22.218
I lose mine all the time.

08:22.718 --> 08:25.638
You lose things, too?

08:26.847 --> 08:28.890
Of course. Why wouldn't I?

08:28.891 --> 08:33.479
Well, you're good at sports and school,
and you even do modeling,

08:34.063 --> 08:36.648
so I kind of just thought
you were perfect.

08:36.649 --> 08:38.566
That's not true.

08:38.567 --> 08:40.527
People say all kinds of stuff,

08:41.403 --> 08:42.863
but really, I'm...

08:44.448 --> 08:47.868
I'm just a normal kid like everyone else.

08:54.500 --> 08:55.793
Watamaki...

08:57.253 --> 08:58.921
SUMIKA WATAMAKI

09:01.048 --> 09:02.967
YUMA
HORNED GREAT HARE - EAST CALCINA PLAINS

09:03.801 --> 09:04.843
Ignis!

09:08.806 --> 09:09.974
Tenebris!

09:11.809 --> 09:13.060
Capere Anima!

09:22.945 --> 09:23.904
Ignis!

09:41.005 --> 09:42.881
SUMIKA WATAMAKI

09:53.976 --> 09:54.893
Yuumy!

09:55.978 --> 09:58.939
Yuumy? Hey! Come on!

10:06.864 --> 10:09.991
Hey, you sure that's safe?

10:09.992 --> 10:12.745
It worked on you, so it should be fine.

10:24.965 --> 10:27.760
Are you okay? Does anything hurt?

10:28.385 --> 10:29.678
Sawa...

10:35.601 --> 10:39.228
That was the Healing Droplet spell, right?

10:39.229 --> 10:41.564
But we're in the real world...

10:41.565 --> 10:45.068
Seriously, Yu?
You still don't get what's going on?

10:45.069 --> 10:47.780
You saw me use Flame Arrow earlier, right?

10:48.447 --> 10:50.574
And look at what you did...

10:57.164 --> 10:59.791
I can't believe you captured her.

10:59.792 --> 11:01.835
Seriously, what's going on?

11:03.253 --> 11:05.338
Konken! You okay?

11:05.339 --> 11:09.175
Yeah, my left arm still hurts a bit, but...

11:09.176 --> 11:11.470
I mean, it felt like it was broken,

11:12.096 --> 11:13.680
but Saps fixed it with magic.

11:15.182 --> 11:18.018
More importantly, is this for real?

11:18.685 --> 11:20.228
You too?

11:20.229 --> 11:23.064
Saps told me to launch Actual Magic,

11:23.065 --> 11:24.607
and it appeared right as I did.

11:24.608 --> 11:27.694
It hurt worse than
when Watamaki hit me.

11:29.196 --> 11:32.240
That was Watamaki, right?

11:32.241 --> 11:35.285
Yeah. That was her.

11:36.578 --> 11:40.248
But she didn't have a face!

11:40.249 --> 11:43.001
Plus, she beat the crap out of us...

11:46.964 --> 11:48.340
Seriously?

11:48.924 --> 11:52.636
Maybe this isn't a dream,
and we really are still in the game.

11:53.220 --> 11:55.096
- Sawa.
- What?

11:55.097 --> 11:58.474
You said earlier
that this is the real world, right?

11:58.475 --> 12:00.852
That if we die here, we die for real.

12:00.853 --> 12:03.646
Did you have a particular reason
for saying that?

12:03.647 --> 12:05.690
Yeah, I do.

12:05.691 --> 12:07.901
You probably already know this, Yu.

12:08.485 --> 12:11.946
The virtual sensations
provided by the Caliculus units

12:11.947 --> 12:13.574
are limited to touch.

12:15.242 --> 12:16.910
Visuals come through the i-Lenses,

12:17.578 --> 12:20.413
and audio is transmitted
through the earpiece,

12:20.414 --> 12:24.625
but taste and smell aren't supported yet.
Which means...

12:24.626 --> 12:26.627
If we can taste or smell anything,

12:26.628 --> 12:29.673
that means we're not in a virtual world.

12:30.924 --> 12:32.885
What's that smell?

12:36.972 --> 12:39.725
So all of this is real?

12:40.309 --> 12:43.436
The i-Lenses and earpieces
seem to be part of us now, too.

12:43.437 --> 12:45.396
So don't try to force them off.

12:45.397 --> 12:48.901
Sawa, how are you so calm about all this?

12:50.194 --> 12:54.697
And not just calm. You seem to know a lot
about what's going on.

12:54.698 --> 12:56.866
Did you know this would happen

12:56.867 --> 12:59.119
when we launched Actual Magic?

12:59.703 --> 13:00.787
Good point.

13:03.790 --> 13:05.625
Of course not!

13:05.626 --> 13:08.545
I tried launching it as a test,
and it just happened.

13:10.589 --> 13:15.093
It's not like I wanted
to look like this, okay?

13:21.141 --> 13:23.018
What are you doing, buttbrain?

13:23.727 --> 13:25.895
I was just curious.

13:25.896 --> 13:29.650
Don't touch me there! It tickles!

13:31.235 --> 13:32.819
What about those wings?

13:39.701 --> 13:41.411
What do we do now?

13:42.746 --> 13:46.415
First, we need to wake Nagi.
Then we decide.

13:46.416 --> 13:48.418
Right. Yeah.

13:56.593 --> 13:58.679
Nagi. Wake up, Nagi.

14:02.224 --> 14:03.684
I think...

14:07.020 --> 14:08.105
Nagi?

14:21.868 --> 14:25.037
The internal emergency release lever
hasn't been used.

14:25.038 --> 14:26.748
That can't be.

14:27.457 --> 14:29.875
Once you use the external lever,

14:29.876 --> 14:33.588
you can't reset it
without restarting the Caliculus.

14:33.589 --> 14:35.047
They told us at orientation.

14:35.048 --> 14:36.091
Yeah.

14:36.633 --> 14:38.551
So, that means...

14:38.552 --> 14:40.511
Until we opened it just now,

14:40.512 --> 14:43.848
there's no way anyone
could have gotten in or out.

14:43.849 --> 14:47.184
What? That can't be right!

14:47.185 --> 14:50.938
Nagi was in the playtest
with the rest of us,

14:50.939 --> 14:53.357
so she had to have been inside.

14:53.358 --> 14:56.903
After we beat that dragon...

14:58.030 --> 15:01.325
<i>I remember the floor
in the boss room turning red.</i>

15:02.034 --> 15:03.952
<i>There was nothing I could do.</i>

15:07.789 --> 15:08.956
<i>Next thing I knew,</i>

15:08.957 --> 15:11.918
<i>I was back inside the Caliculus.</i>

15:13.295 --> 15:15.588
<i>No one came when I called,</i>

15:15.589 --> 15:17.924
<i>so I used the lever to get out.</i>

15:19.676 --> 15:21.136
It was the same for me.

15:21.845 --> 15:24.848
When I got back to reality,
everything was pitch-black...

15:26.933 --> 15:28.352
Yu?

15:32.356 --> 15:34.732
Right before I got out of the capsule,

15:34.733 --> 15:37.194
I thought I heard someone scream.

15:37.819 --> 15:40.029
Was that you, Konken?

15:40.030 --> 15:42.074
Nah, I didn't scream.

15:42.616 --> 15:44.367
Was it a boy or a girl?

15:44.368 --> 15:47.871
It was pretty high-pitched,
but I heard it through the capsule, so...

15:48.580 --> 15:50.040
I see.

15:50.624 --> 15:53.042
Sawa! You don't think
that was Nagi screaming?

15:53.043 --> 15:55.545
Don't ask me! I don't know either!

16:03.053 --> 16:05.304
Actually, I doubt it was her.

16:05.305 --> 16:09.226
Since the lever hasn't been used,
Nagi couldn't have left the capsule.

16:10.143 --> 16:14.313
That would make it impossible
for Watamaki to attack her.

16:14.314 --> 16:17.358
Right. But then how do we explain...

16:17.359 --> 16:19.403
She didn't just vanish into thin air.

16:20.153 --> 16:23.572
She has to be somewhere, right?
She's gotta be.

16:23.573 --> 16:24.825
Yeah.

16:25.659 --> 16:28.327
Yeah. I think so too.

16:28.328 --> 16:31.288
Then we've gotta go find her.

16:31.289 --> 16:33.333
Because Nagimiso's such a crybaby.

16:33.917 --> 16:37.295
When we find her, I'm so telling her
you called her Nagimiso!

16:38.004 --> 16:40.549
Wait! Just forget I ever said it, okay?

16:48.432 --> 16:51.017
I'll go get a teacher!

16:52.352 --> 16:54.228
Apart from searching for Nagi,

16:54.229 --> 16:56.606
can we add one more objective?

16:57.441 --> 16:59.150
While Watamaki is in card form,

16:59.151 --> 17:02.446
I want to find a way
to get her back to normal.

17:03.530 --> 17:04.740
And I need your help.

17:05.407 --> 17:06.867
Of course.

17:07.367 --> 17:10.036
As if we could just leave
Watamaki like that.

17:19.087 --> 17:20.087
What's wrong?

17:20.088 --> 17:21.631
Nothing.

17:22.132 --> 17:23.591
It all makes sense now.

17:23.592 --> 17:25.843
Sumika is a really cute girl.

17:25.844 --> 17:29.597
That's got nothing to do with it!
Not in a situation like this.

17:29.598 --> 17:31.390
I know that.

17:31.391 --> 17:33.559
I want to turn her back too.

17:33.560 --> 17:36.104
So what's the actual plan?

17:38.774 --> 17:41.358
For now, let's head for the lobby
on the first floor.

17:41.359 --> 17:43.903
If anyone else got out of their Caliculus,

17:43.904 --> 17:45.988
they'd probably head back there.

17:45.989 --> 17:47.615
But before that...

17:47.616 --> 17:49.575
We search this room.

17:49.576 --> 17:51.745
There might be some kind of clue.

17:52.496 --> 17:54.121
Yeah. Exactly.

17:54.122 --> 17:55.539
Let's split up.

17:55.540 --> 17:58.417
I'll check over here.
You guys go that way.

17:58.418 --> 18:01.213
Grab anything you find
that we can use as a weapon.

18:05.842 --> 18:08.260
Hey, Saps and Nagimiso

18:08.261 --> 18:10.763
always have this weird look on their faces

18:10.764 --> 18:14.058
when we talk about Watamaki, right?

18:14.059 --> 18:16.436
Even though they're pretty close with her.

18:17.270 --> 18:18.521
Just so you know,

18:18.522 --> 18:21.524
my stats have gone up,
and that includes my hearing!

18:21.525 --> 18:23.109
I'm telling her everything!

18:24.069 --> 18:25.611
I'm gonna check down below.

18:25.612 --> 18:26.696
Okay.

18:36.623 --> 18:39.875
This is... not heavy enough.

18:39.876 --> 18:41.294
That makes sense.

18:42.087 --> 18:43.295
What does?

18:43.296 --> 18:45.005
An equipment overload icon

18:45.006 --> 18:48.009
appeared under my status bar.

18:48.593 --> 18:49.928
Seriously?

19:00.063 --> 19:02.022
Man, this really is a game.

19:02.023 --> 19:05.776
Yeah. It's like reality
is being overwritten

19:05.777 --> 19:08.071
by Actual Magic's game system.

19:08.613 --> 19:11.031
So I'm strong because I'm a warrior?

19:11.032 --> 19:12.784
Yu! Konken!

19:18.123 --> 19:19.291
Sawa?

19:40.395 --> 19:41.605
Sorry.

19:48.028 --> 19:50.739
CLASS 6-1

19:56.786 --> 19:58.246
Not even close!

20:06.421 --> 20:08.757
She ate his heart.

20:13.720 --> 20:15.262
That scream...

20:15.263 --> 20:18.266
It was Miura.

20:19.601 --> 20:21.770
Is that Beroshi?

20:25.941 --> 20:29.277
Did Watamaki kill him?

20:35.033 --> 20:37.284
SUMIKA WATAMAKI
NIGHT FIEND - LEVEL 17

20:37.285 --> 20:40.287
YUKIHISA MIURA'S RIGHT ARM
STRIKE ATTACK 18 - MAGIC ATTACK 3

20:40.288 --> 20:41.830
What the hell?

20:41.831 --> 20:43.917
Beroshi isn't a game character.

20:48.380 --> 20:52.217
Hey, can we at least
give him a better resting place?

21:05.939 --> 21:06.940
What was that?

21:10.944 --> 21:12.070
From below?

21:13.321 --> 21:14.322
Let's go.

21:25.709 --> 21:26.959
Why...

21:26.960 --> 21:31.964
YUMA ASHIHARA
ALTHEA 1F

21:31.965 --> 21:35.301
What is this? What's going on?

21:49.774 --> 21:51.358
What is that thing?

21:51.359 --> 21:53.903
Why is there a monster here?

23:27.997 --> 23:28.831
AWAKENING

23:28.832 --> 23:30.749
<i>Think. How can we beat it?</i>

23:30.750 --> 23:32.251
<i>Over here, monster!</i>

23:32.252 --> 23:34.002
<i>Am I... dead?</i>

23:34.003 --> 23:35.462
<i>All right, leave this to me!</i>

23:35.463 --> 23:37.256
<i>The thread of life is connected.</i>

23:37.257 --> 23:39.591
<i>I don't want to regret it
when it's too late!</i>

23:39.592 --> 23:42.929
<i>Are you really Sawa?</i>
